   "symbol": "AAPL",
   "role": "news",
   "text": "Apple reports fiscal fourth-quarter results on 29 October after the close. Supplier commentary from Taiwan points to steady iPhone 18 builds through December, and two outlets report expanded production of the base model. On the macro side, the Federal Reserve meets on 4 November with futures pricing a 25 bp cut, and ten-year Treasury yields eased to 4.0% over the week. A European Commission decision on App Store fees remains pending; reports describe a fine range but no date. Insider activity was routine, with two Form 4 sales under 10b5-1 plans.\n\n| Item | Date | Relevance |\n|---|---|---|\n| Q4 FY26 results | 29 Oct | Near-term catalyst |\n| FOMC decision | 4 Nov | Rates backdrop |\n| EU App Store ruling | Pending | Regulatory overhang |",
   "forced": false
