   "symbol": "AAPL",
   "role": "market",
   "text": "AAPL closed the week at $347.73 on Friday 23 October, up 5.3% across the month after a run of higher lows since early October. The 50-day SMA sits near $336 and the 200-day near $312, so price trades above both averages and the 50-day keeps rising. RSI(14) read 61 at Friday's close, below the 70 line that marks a stretched move. MACD stays above its signal line, though the histogram has narrowed for three sessions, which says momentum is slowing rather than reversing. ATR(14) is about $6.10, roughly 1.8% of price. Volume on the rally days ran near the 30-day average, without a climactic spike.\n\n| Indicator | Reading | What it says |\n|---|---|---|\n| Close vs 50/200 SMA | Above both | Uptrend intact |\n| RSI(14) | 61 | Firm, not stretched |\n| MACD histogram | Narrowing | Momentum slowing |\n| ATR(14) | $6.10 | Daily range near 1.8% |",
   "forced": false
