   "symbol": "AAPL",
   "role": "fundamentals",
   "text": "Apple's trailing revenue stands near $416 billion with a gross margin of 46.9% and an operating margin of 32.6%. Services carry a higher margin than hardware and now contribute roughly a quarter of revenue. The trailing P/E is about 39.8 and the forward P/E about 36.3, both above the five-year median near 29. Return on equity is very high because buybacks keep the equity base small. The quarterly balance sheet was unavailable this run (none of the statement vendors answered), so leverage figures come from the key-metrics feed: debt to equity of 78% and a current ratio of 1.0.\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Gross margin | 46.9% |\n| Operating margin | 32.6% |\n| Trailing P/E | 39.8 |\n| Forward P/E | 36.3 |\n| Debt to equity | 78% |",
